/* Airline Agent Policy — tau2-airline
   Source spec: experiments/translation/spec.md
   Trace evidence: outputs/variant-set/run1/scenarios.json (95 captured,
   oracle-labeled decision points) and outputs/variant-set/run1/system.md.

   Mode L (trace-grounded). Content checks use custom C++ functors
   declared below and implemented in airline_functors.cpp — no
   @llm_check_fn, no @ask, no ActionMetadata (see "Deployment
   constructs" note at the end of the spec block).

   Round-trip audit: PASS (2026-08-20)
*/
#include "../../../../policies/common_policy.dl"

/* ── K-Constraints (verified against outputs/variant-set/run1) ──────

   K1: The capture records every conversation TWICE, mirrored. Under
       msg.agent = "LLMAgent" the CUSTOMER speaks with
       msg.agent_role = $UserRole(); under msg.agent = "UserSimulator"
       the roles are swapped, so UserSimulator/$UserRole() carries the
       AGENT's own words. Evidence: node
       245c98f3-2cc6-4e1b-8fc9-651ad569e4ab is
       (agent="UserSimulator", role=user, contents="Hi! How can I help
       you today?"). Both names appear in the backward slice of every
       decision point (333 UserSimulator/user nodes across the 95
       slices). Therefore EVERY rule that reads customer text filters
       msg.agent = "LLMAgent" AND msg.agent_role = $UserRole(); a rule
       keyed on the role alone lets the agent confirm its own writes.

   K2: Tool results are attributed to msg.agent = "LLMAgent" with
       msg.agent_role = $AgentType(), and carry the result payload in
       msg.contents. They are also marked by ToolResult(id, fn, args).
       ToolResult facts ARE present in this capture (80 of 95 slices
       carry at least one), so attribute rules that join on them are
       live, not vacuous.

   K3: get_user_details results carry "membership" as a bare top-level
       string ("regular" | "silver" | "gold") and "payment_methods" as
       a top-level OBJECT keyed by payment id — hence
       @json_object_has_key(contents, "payment_methods", pid) rather
       than an array scan.

   K4: get_reservation_details results carry top-level "reservation_id",
       "user_id", "origin", "destination", "flight_type", "cabin",
       "insurance" ("yes"/"no"), "created_at", "total_baggages",
       "nonfree_baggages", and arrays "flights" (each leg with
       flight_number/origin/destination/date/price) and "passengers".
       update_reservation_flights / update_reservation_passengers /
       cancel_reservation return the SAME payload shape on success and a
       bare "Error: ..." string on failure (which parses to nothing, so
       a failed write contributes no facts).

   K5: search_direct_flight and search_onestop_flight return top-level
       JSON ARRAYS, so no top-level field accessor works on them. The
       only way to resolve a proposed flight number's airports is a
       scanning functor (@flight_origin / @flight_destination), which
       walks to the enclosing object wherever the leg sits.

   K6: Every direct inbound edge into a Current node carries an EdgeData
       tuple with a >= 0 message_index (checked on all 23 write-tool
       decision points: 0 missing). "The customer's latest turn" is
       therefore the LLMAgent/$UserRole() source with the greatest
       message_index into Current. All direct inbound edges come from
       LLMAgent, never UserSimulator — the agent filter is still applied
       per K1 rather than relying on that.

   K7: Slices are small (7-66 nodes, at most 2 agent names), so scanning
       every slice message with a functor is affordable. CurrentDepends
       is gated to the six write tools; read-only tools never consult
       prior graph state.

   K8: The capture carries no roles (provenance.roles_unknown = true,
       roles: []) and the airline spec defines no roles, so this policy
       contains no RBAC clause. principal is "captured-principal", so
       HasPrincipal() holds.
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Structured Spec ────────────────────────────────────────────────

   C1:  Authorize airline agent tool calls by default; deny by exception.
   C2:  Return an error (not a pass-through) when an action is denied.

   Confirmation before database writes
   C3:  Deny book_reservation, update_reservation_flights,
        update_reservation_baggages, update_reservation_passengers and
        cancel_reservation when the customer's LATEST turn does not
        explicitly confirm going ahead with the action.

   Modify flight
   C4:  Deny update_reservation_flights on a reservation whose current
        cabin is basic economy when the proposed leg list differs from
        the booked one (basic economy flights cannot be modified; a
        pure cabin change on the same legs is allowed).
   C5:  Deny update_reservation_flights whose new itinerary does not
        end at the reservation's booked destination.
   C6:  Deny update_reservation_flights whose new itinerary does not
        start at the reservation's booked origin.
   C7:  Deny update_reservation_flights when any booked leg has already
        departed (cabin cannot change once a flight has been flown).
   C8:  Deny update_reservation_flights / update_reservation_passengers
        / update_reservation_baggages / cancel_reservation for a
        reservation whose details were never retrieved in this
        conversation (the API does not check the rules for the agent).
   C9:  Deny update_reservation_passengers that changes the NUMBER of
        passengers.
   C10: Deny update_reservation_baggages that reduces the checked-bag
        count (bags may be added, never removed).
   C11: Deny a write whose payment_id is absent from the customer's
        retrieved profile (payment methods must already be on file).

   Cancel flight
   C12: Deny cancel_reservation when no reason for cancellation has been
        given by the customer.
   C13: Deny cancel_reservation when any leg has already been flown
        (transfer to a human agent is required instead).
   C14: Deny cancel_reservation unless at least one eligibility ground
        holds: booked within the last 24 h, airline-cancelled flight,
        business cabin, or travel insurance plus a covered reason.

   Book flight
   C15: Deny book_reservation with more than five passengers.
   C16: Deny book_reservation using more than one travel certificate,
        more than one credit card, or more than three gift cards.
   C17: Deny book_reservation whose payment ids are absent from the
        retrieved profile.

   Refunds and compensation
   C18: Deny send_certificate when the recipient's membership level has
        not been verified in this conversation.
   C19: Deny send_certificate to a regular member.
   C20: Deny send_certificate when the customer never asked for
        compensation (no proactive offers).
   C21: Deny send_certificate whose amount is neither $50 nor $100 per
        passenger on the affected reservation.

   Graph assumptions per clause, all confirmed against the run1 traces:
   C3 reads the latest customer turn via EdgeData ordering (K6). C4-C11
   and C13-C14, C18-C21 read tool-result payloads reached through
   CurrentDepends (K2, K4). C5/C6 additionally resolve airports from any
   payload in the slice (K5).

   Spec statements deliberately NOT encoded, with the reason:
   - "list the action details" is enforced only through its observable
     half (C3, explicit confirmation). Whether the agent enumerated the
     details is not decidable from the graph.
   - "only one tool call at a time / no message plus tool call": the
     capture shows a single assistant message emitting three writes
     whose decision points the oracle then labels differently
     (update_reservation_flights-38c2e7df allowed,
     update_reservation_passengers-dc79486c denied), so multiplicity is
     not itself the violation and a rule on it would deny allowed work.
   - free checked-bag allowance by membership x cabin: the traces show
     over-charging bag calls being allowed
     (update_reservation_baggages-e476078c and -ef3e4c90 bill a gold
     member for three non-free bags), so an allowance rule would deny
     approved traffic. Left unenforced rather than encoded wrongly.
   - "cannot add insurance after booking" and "cabin must match across
     legs": neither update tool takes an insurance flag or a per-leg
     cabin, so the API surface already makes these unrepresentable. A
     rule would be dead code.
   - trip-type preservation: update_reservation_flights carries no
     flight_type argument, and one-way/round-trip cannot be inferred
     from the leg list alone without the booked route, which C5/C6
     already pin.
   - "no information beyond the tools", "no subjective recommendations",
     "transfer only when out of scope": properties of message text the
     agent sends, not of the tool calls this monitor sees.

   Deployment constructs: no @ask (the tau2 harness has no approval
   channel — an ask-kind reason would be indistinguishable from an
   allow), no @llm_check_fn (no oracle configured for this run), no
   ActionMetadata (the tau2 SDK call site passes no metadata, so the
   relation is permanently empty).
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Known limitations ──────────────────────────────────────────────

   L1: "Now" is the spec's stated current time (2024-05-15 15:00:00),
       written as a fact. Against a real clock these dates are wrong and
       the flown-leg and 24-hour rules would need the time supplied per
       request.

   L2: Confirmation (C3), a cancellation reason (C12) and a compensation
       request (C20) are decided by phrase matching over customer text.
       The phrase tables are drawn from the language in this capture; a
       customer who confirms in wording the tables do not carry is
       denied, and would need the tables extended. Every such rule
       denies rather than allows on a miss, so the failure direction is
       to block work, never to wave a write through.

   L3: The cancellation grounds that come from the conversation
       ("the airline cancelled my flight", a covered reason) are read
       across the whole slice, not tied to one reservation id. In a
       conversation about several reservations, such a statement
       unlocks cancelling any of them that the other rules permit. The
       grounds that come from the reservation payload (business cabin,
       insurance flag, 24-hour window) are correctly per-reservation.

   L4: When a conversation performs two or more SUCCESSFUL
       update_reservation_flights calls on one reservation, the leg
       lists of every successful result are in scope at once, because
       ordering them would need pairwise ReachableFrom. Only C4 reads
       leg lists, and C4 additionally requires the cabin to still be
       basic economy — a state the earlier updates cannot leave behind
       — so no rule is known to misfire from this. It is an ordering
       gap, not an observed defect.

   L5: A payment id counts as on file if ANY profile fetched in the
       conversation carries it (C11, C17); the policy does not check
       that the profile belongs to the reservation's owner.

   L6: The free checked-bag allowance and the flown-flight rules read
       fields that are present in every observed payload but are not
       guaranteed. Where a field is missing the rules stand down rather
       than deny — except C9 and C10, where a malformed call carrying
       no passenger list or no bag count is denied on purpose.
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   CUSTOM FUNCTOR DECLARATIONS (airline_functors.cpp)
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* Explicit confirmation to proceed with the proposed action. */
.functor user_confirms_action(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
/* Any stated reason for wanting to cancel. */
.functor cancellation_reason_stated(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
/* A reason travel insurance covers (health / weather / significant
   personal circumstances). */
.functor covered_cancellation_reason(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
/* The AIRLINE cancelled the flight (as opposed to the customer). */
.functor airline_cancelled_flight(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
/* The customer asked for compensation themselves. */
.functor user_requested_compensation(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
/* Resolve a flight number's airports from any payload that describes
   it — search results are top-level arrays, so no path accessor works
   (K5). */
.functor flight_origin(json: symbol, flight_num: symbol): symbol stateful
.functor flight_destination(json: symbol, flight_num: symbol): symbol stateful
/* ISO date comparison. Souffle orders symbols by symbol-table index,
   not lexicographically, so date ordering needs a functor. */
.functor date_before(a: symbol, b: symbol): unsigned stateful
/* Count payment ids with a given prefix in a book_reservation call. */
.functor count_payment_prefix(json: symbol, prefix: symbol): number stateful

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   DEFAULT AUTHORIZATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C1: the agent's tool calls are allowed unless a rule below denies. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :- Actions(idx, _).

/* C2: a denial is an error, not a silent pass-through. */
DenyUnauthorized(idx) :- Actions(idx, _).

/* Only the write tools consult prior graph state; gating the traversal
   keeps read-only calls (get_*, search_*, calculate,
   transfer_to_human_agents) from paying for CurrentDepends at all.
   ReachableFrom is never used, so its gate stays unset. */
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "book_reservation").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_flights").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_baggages").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_passengers").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "cancel_reservation").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "send_certificate").

/* Leg / passenger positions. Reservations hold at most a handful of
   legs and at most five passengers; 16 covers both with margin. */
.decl Indices(i: unsigned)
Indices(0).
Indices(i + 1) :- Indices(i), i < 16.

/* The spec's stated current time, used for "already flown" and the
   24-hour booking window. */
.decl Now(ts: symbol)
Now("2024-05-15T15:00:00").
.decl Today(d: symbol)
Today("2024-05-15").

/* Tools that write to the booking database. */
.decl WriteTool(name: symbol)
WriteTool("book_reservation").
WriteTool("update_reservation_flights").
WriteTool("update_reservation_baggages").
WriteTool("update_reservation_passengers").
WriteTool("cancel_reservation").

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   CONVERSATION HELPERS
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* A customer turn feeding the action under evaluation, with its
   position in the agent's input history. K1: the msg.agent filter is
   what separates the real customer from the mirrored UserSimulator
   copy, which carries the AGENT's own words. */
.decl CustomerTurn(id: symbol, i: number)
CustomerTurn(id, i) :-
    Current(cur),
    EdgeData(id, cur, data),
    i = data.message_index,
    i >= 0,
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole().

.decl CustomerTurnSuperseded(id: symbol)
CustomerTurnSuperseded(id) :-
    CustomerTurn(id, i),
    CustomerTurn(_, j),
    j > i.

/* The customer's most recent turn — the one the agent is acting on. */
.decl LatestCustomerTurn(id: symbol)
LatestCustomerTurn(id) :-
    CustomerTurn(id, _),
    !CustomerTurnSuperseded(id).

/* Any customer turn anywhere in the backward slice. Used where the
   spec asks whether something was ever stated (a cancellation reason,
   a compensation request) rather than what the customer just said. */
.decl CustomerSaid(id: symbol)
CustomerSaid(id) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole().

/* C3 support: the latest turn explicitly confirms proceeding. */
.decl ActionConfirmed()
ActionConfirmed() :-
    LatestCustomerTurn(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @user_confirms_action(msg.contents) = 1.

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   RESERVATION AND PROFILE DATA (from tool results)
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* A reservation payload reached from the current action. Successful
   writes echo the same shape, so a post-write payload is as good a
   source as the original lookup; a failed write returns "Error: ..."
   which parses to nothing and contributes no facts (K4). */
.decl ReservationPayload(res_id: symbol, body: symbol)
ReservationPayload(res_id, body) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, tool, _),
    ReservationReturningTool(tool),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    body = msg.contents,
    res_id = @json_get_str(body, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "".

.decl ReservationReturningTool(name: symbol)
ReservationReturningTool("get_reservation_details").
ReservationReturningTool("update_reservation_flights").
ReservationReturningTool("update_reservation_passengers").
ReservationReturningTool("update_reservation_baggages").
ReservationReturningTool("cancel_reservation").

/* C8 support: the reservation was actually looked up. */
.decl ReservationRetrieved(res_id: symbol)
ReservationRetrieved(res_id) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, "get_reservation_details", _),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    res_id = @json_get_str(msg.contents, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "".

/* A write that succeeded supersedes the original lookup, so the cabin
   and leg list read below are the post-write ones. Without this, a
   reservation whose cabin was upgraded would still carry its old
   basic-economy cabin and a later call would be denied on stale data. */
.decl ReservationUpdated(res_id: symbol, body: symbol)
ReservationUpdated(res_id, body) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, "update_reservation_flights", _),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    body = msg.contents,
    res_id = @json_get_str(body, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "".

.decl FreshReservation(res_id: symbol, body: symbol)
FreshReservation(res_id, body) :- ReservationUpdated(res_id, body).
FreshReservation(res_id, body) :-
    ReservationPayload(res_id, body),
    !ReservationUpdated(res_id, _).

.decl ReservationCabin(res_id: symbol, cabin: symbol)
ReservationCabin(res_id, cabin) :-
    FreshReservation(res_id, body),
    cabin = @json_get_str(body, "cabin"),
    cabin != "".

.decl ReservationRoute(res_id: symbol, origin: symbol, dest: symbol)
ReservationRoute(res_id, origin, dest) :-
    ReservationPayload(res_id, body),
    origin = @json_get_str(body, "origin"),
    origin != "",
    dest = @json_get_str(body, "destination"),
    dest != "".

.decl ReservationInsured(res_id: symbol)
ReservationInsured(res_id) :-
    ReservationPayload(res_id, body),
    "yes" = @json_get_str(body, "insurance").

.decl ReservationCreatedAt(res_id: symbol, ts: symbol)
ReservationCreatedAt(res_id, ts) :-
    ReservationPayload(res_id, body),
    ts = @json_get_str(body, "created_at"),
    ts != "".

.decl ReservationBags(res_id: symbol, total: number)
ReservationBags(res_id, total) :-
    FreshReservation(res_id, body),
    total = @json_get_int(body, "total_baggages"),
    total >= 0.

.decl ReservationPassengerCount(res_id: symbol, n: unsigned)
ReservationPassengerCount(res_id, n) :-
    FreshReservation(res_id, body),
    n = @json_array_len(body, "passengers"),
    n > 0.

/* Booked legs, position-indexed. "flights" is an array, so only the
   array accessor reaches inside it (a top-level @json_get_str would
   silently return "" and every rule below it would be dead). */
.decl BookedLeg(res_id: symbol, i: unsigned, flight_num: symbol)
BookedLeg(res_id, i, flight_num) :-
    FreshReservation(res_id, body),
    Indices(i),
    flight_num = @json_array_get_field_str(body, "flights", i, "flight_number"),
    flight_num != "".

.decl BookedLegCount(res_id: symbol, n: unsigned)
BookedLegCount(res_id, n) :-
    FreshReservation(res_id, body),
    n = @json_array_len(body, "flights"),
    n > 0.

.decl BookedLegDate(res_id: symbol, flight_num: symbol, d: symbol)
BookedLegDate(res_id, flight_num, d) :-
    FreshReservation(res_id, body),
    Indices(i),
    flight_num = @json_array_get_field_str(body, "flights", i, "flight_number"),
    flight_num != "",
    d = @json_array_get_field_str(body, "flights", i, "date"),
    d != "".

/* C7 / C13 support: a leg dated before today has departed. Same-day
   legs are treated as not yet flown — the payload carries a date but no
   departure time, so blocking them would deny work the spec permits. */
.decl ReservationHasFlownLeg(res_id: symbol)
ReservationHasFlownLeg(res_id) :-
    BookedLegDate(res_id, _, d),
    Today(today),
    @date_before(d, today) = 1.

/* Membership level, keyed by the user it was fetched for (K3). */
.decl UserMembership(user_id: symbol, level: symbol)
UserMembership(user_id, level) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, "get_user_details", _),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    user_id = @json_get_str(msg.contents, "user_id"),
    user_id != "",
    level = @json_get_str(msg.contents, "membership"),
    level != "".

/* Payment methods on file. payment_methods is an OBJECT keyed by
   payment id, so key membership is the right test (K3). */
.decl ProfileRetrieved()
ProfileRetrieved() :- UserMembership(_, _).

.decl PaymentOnFile(payment_id: symbol)
PaymentOnFile(payment_id) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, "get_user_details", _),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    PaymentIdInPlay(payment_id),
    @json_object_has_key(msg.contents, "payment_methods", payment_id) = 1.

/* The payment ids this request would actually charge — bound first so
   the object-key probe above has something to look for. */
.decl PaymentIdInPlay(payment_id: symbol)
PaymentIdInPlay(payment_id) :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsToolCall(a),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    payment_id = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    payment_id != "".
PaymentIdInPlay(payment_id) :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    Indices(i),
    payment_id = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "payment_methods", i, "payment_id"),
    payment_id != "".

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   PROPOSED ITINERARY (update_reservation_flights arguments)
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.decl ProposedLeg(res_id: symbol, i: unsigned, flight_num: symbol)
ProposedLeg(res_id, i, flight_num) :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    Indices(i),
    flight_num = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "flights", i, "flight_number"),
    flight_num != "".

.decl ProposedLegCount(res_id: symbol, n: unsigned)
ProposedLegCount(res_id, n) :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    n = @json_array_len(args, "flights"),
    n > 0.

/* C4 support: does the call actually move the flights, or only the
   cabin? Position-wise difference, plus a length check. */
.decl FlightsBeingChanged(res_id: symbol)
FlightsBeingChanged(res_id) :-
    ProposedLeg(res_id, i, new_flight),
    BookedLeg(res_id, i, old_flight),
    new_flight != old_flight.
FlightsBeingChanged(res_id) :-
    ProposedLegCount(res_id, new_len),
    BookedLegCount(res_id, old_len),
    new_len != old_len.

/* C5 / C6 support: the airports of each proposed leg, resolved from
   whatever payload in the slice describes that flight — a search
   result, or the reservation itself when the leg is being kept (K5). */
.decl ProposedLegOrigin(res_id: symbol, i: unsigned, airport: symbol)
ProposedLegOrigin(res_id, i, airport) :-
    ProposedLeg(res_id, i, flight_num),
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    airport = @flight_origin(msg.contents, flight_num),
    airport != "".

.decl ProposedLegDest(res_id: symbol, i: unsigned, airport: symbol)
ProposedLegDest(res_id, i, airport) :-
    ProposedLeg(res_id, i, flight_num),
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    airport = @flight_destination(msg.contents, flight_num),
    airport != "".

/* If any proposed leg's airports cannot be resolved, the route checks
   stand down rather than guess — an unresolvable leg could be the one
   that reaches the booked destination. */
.decl UnresolvedProposedLeg(res_id: symbol)
UnresolvedProposedLeg(res_id) :-
    ProposedLeg(res_id, i, _),
    !ProposedLegDest(res_id, i, _).
UnresolvedProposedLeg(res_id) :-
    ProposedLeg(res_id, i, _),
    !ProposedLegOrigin(res_id, i, _).

.decl ProposedItineraryReachesDest(res_id: symbol)
ProposedItineraryReachesDest(res_id) :-
    ReservationRoute(res_id, _, dest),
    ProposedLegDest(res_id, _, dest).

.decl ProposedItineraryStartsAtOrigin(res_id: symbol)
ProposedItineraryStartsAtOrigin(res_id) :-
    ReservationRoute(res_id, origin, _),
    ProposedLegOrigin(res_id, 0, origin).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C3 — EXPLICIT CONFIRMATION BEFORE ANY DATABASE WRITE
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C3: "Before taking any actions that update the booking database ...
   you must list the action details and obtain explicit user
   confirmation (yes) to proceed." Judged on the customer's latest turn:
   a confirmation that predates a fresh instruction is not a
   confirmation of the fresh instruction. */
// @deny_message: This booking change was not confirmed by the customer. Their most recent message does not agree to proceed with these details.
// @suggestion: List the exact action details (flights, cabin, passengers, bags, amounts and payment method) and ask the customer to confirm with a clear "yes" before calling this tool again.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, tool),
    WriteTool(tool),
    !ActionConfirmed().

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C4-C7 — MODIFYING FLIGHTS
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C4: "Basic economy flights cannot be modified", read together with
   "all reservations, including basic economy, can change cabin without
   changing the flights" — so the deny is on moving the legs, not on
   touching a basic-economy reservation at all. */
// @deny_message: Basic economy reservations cannot have their flights changed.
// @suggestion: Only a cabin change is possible on a basic economy booking; keep the same flight segments, or explain that the customer would have to cancel and rebook if they are eligible.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    ReservationCabin(res_id, "basic_economy"),
    FlightsBeingChanged(res_id).

/* C5: "Other reservations can be modified without changing the origin,
   destination, and trip type." */
// @deny_message: This change would alter the reservation's destination.
// @suggestion: A reservation can only be re-routed between the same origin and destination. Offer flights that still end at the booked destination airport.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    ReservationRoute(res_id, _, _),
    ProposedLeg(res_id, _, _),
    !UnresolvedProposedLeg(res_id),
    !ProposedItineraryReachesDest(res_id).

/* C6: same clause, origin side. */
// @deny_message: This change would alter the reservation's origin.
// @suggestion: Keep the first segment departing from the booked origin airport, or cancel and rebook if the customer is eligible.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    ReservationRoute(res_id, _, _),
    ProposedLeg(res_id, 0, _),
    !UnresolvedProposedLeg(res_id),
    !ProposedItineraryStartsAtOrigin(res_id).

/* C7: "Cabin cannot be changed if any flight in the reservation has
   already been flown." */
// @deny_message: This reservation already has a flown segment, so its flights and cabin can no longer be changed.
// @suggestion: Explain that the trip is partly flown and transfer to a human agent if the customer needs more help.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    ReservationHasFlownLeg(res_id).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C8-C11 — VERIFY BEFORE WRITING
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C8: "The API does not check these for the agent, so the agent must
   make sure the rules apply before calling the API." Nothing about a
   reservation can be checked before it has been read. */
// @deny_message: This reservation's details have not been retrieved in this conversation, so its rules cannot have been checked.
// @suggestion: Call get_reservation_details for this reservation id first, verify the change is permitted, then retry.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, tool),
    ReservationScopedTool(tool),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    !ReservationRetrieved(res_id).

.decl ReservationScopedTool(name: symbol)
ReservationScopedTool("update_reservation_flights").
ReservationScopedTool("update_reservation_baggages").
ReservationScopedTool("update_reservation_passengers").
ReservationScopedTool("cancel_reservation").

/* C9: "The user can modify passengers but cannot modify the number of
   passengers. Even a human agent cannot modify the number of
   passengers." */
// @deny_message: A reservation's passenger count cannot be changed.
// @suggestion: Submit the same number of passengers as the booking holds; a different headcount needs a new reservation.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_passengers"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    n = @json_array_len(args, "passengers"),
    ReservationPassengerCount(res_id, booked),
    n != booked.

/* C10: "The user can add but not remove checked bags." */
// @deny_message: Checked bags cannot be removed from a reservation.
// @suggestion: total_baggages must be at least the number already on the booking; bags can only be added.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_baggages"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    proposed = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    ReservationBags(res_id, booked),
    proposed < booked.

/* C11: "All payment methods must already be in user profile for safety
   reasons." Only enforced once a profile has actually been fetched —
   with no profile in the slice there is nothing to check the id
   against, and denying then would block work the traces show being
   allowed. */
// @deny_message: That payment method is not on the customer's profile.
// @suggestion: Use a payment method returned by get_user_details for this customer; new cards cannot be charged.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, tool),
    WriteTool(tool),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    payment_id = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    payment_id != "",
    ProfileRetrieved(),
    !PaymentOnFile(payment_id).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C12-C14 — CANCELLING
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.decl CancellationReasonGiven()
CancellationReasonGiven() :-
    CustomerSaid(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @cancellation_reason_stated(msg.contents) = 1.

/* C12: "The agent must also obtain the reason for cancellation." */
// @deny_message: The customer has not given a reason for cancelling.
// @suggestion: Ask why they want to cancel — change of plan, an airline-cancelled flight, or another reason — before calling cancel_reservation.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    !CancellationReasonGiven().

/* C13: "If any portion of the flight has already been flown, the agent
   cannot help and transfer is needed." */
// @deny_message: Part of this trip has already been flown, so it cannot be cancelled here.
// @suggestion: Transfer the customer to a human agent with transfer_to_human_agents.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    ReservationHasFlownLeg(res_id).

/* C14 support: the four grounds the spec allows a cancellation on. */
.decl CancellationAllowed(res_id: symbol)

/* Booked within the last 24 hours. */
CancellationAllowed(res_id) :-
    ReservationCreatedAt(res_id, created),
    Now(now),
    hours = @hours_between(created, now),
    hours >= 0,
    hours <= 24.

/* A business-cabin reservation. */
CancellationAllowed(res_id) :-
    ReservationCabin(res_id, "business").

/* The airline cancelled the flight, as stated by the customer. */
CancellationAllowed(res_id) :-
    ReservationPayload(res_id, _),
    CustomerSaid(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @airline_cancelled_flight(msg.contents) = 1.

/* Travel insurance plus a covered reason. */
CancellationAllowed(res_id) :-
    ReservationInsured(res_id),
    CustomerSaid(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @covered_cancellation_reason(msg.contents) = 1.

/* C14: cancellation needs one of those grounds. */
// @deny_message: This reservation does not meet any cancellation rule — it was not booked in the last 24 hours, is not a business booking, was not cancelled by the airline, and has no insurance covering the stated reason.
// @suggestion: Check created_at, the cabin, and the insurance flag on the reservation, and confirm the customer's reason. If none of the grounds apply, explain that and offer a transfer to a human agent.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    res_id = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    res_id != "",
    !CancellationAllowed(res_id).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C15-C17 — BOOKING
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C15: "Each reservation can have at most five passengers." */
// @deny_message: A reservation may hold at most five passengers.
// @suggestion: Split the party across more than one reservation.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @json_array_len(args, "passengers"),
    n > 5.

/* C16: "Each reservation can use at most one travel certificate, at
   most one credit card, and at most three gift cards." */
// @deny_message: A booking may use at most one travel certificate.
// @suggestion: Use a single certificate and cover the rest with a credit card or gift cards.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "certificate"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A booking may use at most one credit card.
// @suggestion: Charge a single credit card and split any remainder onto gift cards or a certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "credit_card"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A booking may use at most three gift cards.
// @suggestion: Use no more than three gift cards and cover the remainder with a credit card or certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "gift_card"),
    n > 3.

/* C17: the same profile requirement as C11, for the payment_methods
   array a booking carries. Guarded on a fetched profile for the same
   reason. */
// @deny_message: One of the payment methods for this booking is not on the customer's profile.
// @suggestion: Pay only with methods returned by get_user_details for this customer.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    Indices(i),
    payment_id = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "payment_methods", i, "payment_id"),
    payment_id != "",
    ProfileRetrieved(),
    !PaymentOnFile(payment_id).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C18-C21 — REFUNDS AND COMPENSATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C18: "Always verify membership level before offering any
   compensation." */
// @deny_message: The customer's membership level has not been verified, so compensation cannot be offered.
// @suggestion: Call get_user_details for this customer and check the membership field before sending a certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    user_id = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    user_id != "",
    !UserMembership(user_id, _).

/* C19: "Regular members are NOT eligible for any compensation,
   regardless of cabin class, travel insurance, or reason." */
// @deny_message: Regular members are not eligible for compensation.
// @suggestion: Only silver and gold members can receive a certificate. Tell the customer their membership level does not qualify.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    user_id = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    user_id != "",
    UserMembership(user_id, "regular").

/* C20: "Do not proactively offer a compensation unless the user
   explicitly asks for one." */
// @deny_message: The customer has not asked for compensation, so none may be offered.
// @suggestion: Do not raise compensation yourself. Send a certificate only after the customer requests one.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !CompensationRequested().

.decl CompensationRequested()
CompensationRequested() :-
    CustomerSaid(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @user_requested_compensation(msg.contents) = 1.

/* C21: "$100 times the number of passengers" for a cancelled flight,
   "$50 per passenger" for a delayed one. Any other amount is not a
   rate the spec authorises. Only checked when a reservation in this
   conversation pins the passenger count. */
.decl CompensationAmountAllowed(amount: number)
CompensationAmountAllowed(amount) :-
    ReservationPassengerCount(_, n),
    amount = 50 * as(n, number).
CompensationAmountAllowed(amount) :-
    ReservationPassengerCount(_, n),
    amount = 100 * as(n, number).

.decl PassengerCountKnown()
PassengerCountKnown() :- ReservationPassengerCount(_, _).

// @deny_message: That certificate amount does not match the authorised rate.
// @suggestion: Compensation is $50 per passenger for a confirmed delay and $100 per passenger for an airline-cancelled flight. Recompute the amount from the reservation's passenger count.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    amount = @json_get_int(args, "amount"),
    amount > 0,
    PassengerCountKnown(),
    !CompensationAmountAllowed(amount).
